# FFTW 3.3.8 (Ubuntu 22.04 libfftw3-single3 3.3.8-2ubuntu8): only a host whose
# radiod links fftw-3.3.8 can import it; find_bundle skips it elsewhere (#114).
#
# Planned ON a 5850U, bare metal (VK5ARG, RAC 137, koch-wsprdaemon, Ubuntu
# 22.04.5), with sigmond's tuning in place: radiod's FFT core (CPU 14) under
# isolcpus/nohz_full/rcu_nocbs=14-15, every movable IRQ herded to CPUs 0-1,
# L3 CAT 10 of 16 ways (03ff = 10 MB) for CPUs 14-15 via sigmond-l3-cat
# (#111), radiod cores capped at 3.2 GHz (turbostat: 100 % busy at 3093 MHz),
# the station suspended (smd admin wisdom suspend).  Made with
# 'smd admin wisdom plan --fresh' (fftwf-wisdom -n -T 1, pinned to CPU 14):
# all 166 transforms measured here, nothing imported.
# Run time 2 h 46 m 20 s (2026-11-14 20:50:56Z - 23:37:18Z); rof3240000
# alone ~70 min (22:27:03 - 23:37:18).
#
# radiod_l3_bytes is the sysfs L3 (16 MB), exactly what radiod_placement()
# reports on a 5850U, because wisdom_verdict() compares the two: any other
# value would make every seeded 5850U replan from scratch.  radiod's real
# share under CAT is radiod_cat_l3_bytes (10 MB), which nothing compares yet
# (#111 open question).
#
# Converged: radiod (ka9q-radio aa52698c) imported it at the 2026-11-15
# 00:32Z boot and /var/lib/ka9q-radio/fft.log stayed UNMODIFIED for the
# following 50+ minutes of decoding (WSPR 15-19 spots/cycle, ~370 FT8/FT4).
